[h1]Seas & Islands[/h1]

West of the Old World lies a New World that the sea has carved into islands, peninsulas and deep, winding bays. Nothing here is one great continent: roughly a third of the map is land, but the water reaches almost every part of it. Ships, ports and sea lanes matter here as much as armies.

Explore from the Old World or start as a native country in a world already home to hundreds of states and tribes.

[h2]🌎 What awaits you[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]A world of islands and inlets:[/b] Ragged coasts, straits and inland seas break the land into many islands and peninsulas of every size. More than half of the 7,272 locations are ports (3,874), so whoever commands the channels shapes every campaign.
[*][b]Open ocean all around:[/b] The oceans are expanded across the Pacific and Atlantic. All 49 vanilla island groups stay in the open sea, and 33 of them are moved to new waters.
[*][b]An inhabited New World:[/b] 197 native states and 593 tribes, with their own cultures, religions and relationships. You can lead one of them or encounter them as an overseas power.
[*][b]Powers to reckon with:[/b] One great empire of 39 locations, Iaguaty, well beyond the largest native state of the vanilla Americas (23); a highland confederation of three tribes; six regional powers; and eight holy sites among the native religions.
[*][b]Rivers, lakes and varied terrain:[/b] The generated lands contain 7,272 land locations, 533 lakes and 1,123 rivers that each reach the sea, with climates, river systems and sea routes shaped around the new geography.
[*][b]Resources worth seeking:[/b] Gold, silver, gems and pearls occur at their vanilla frequency, and five exceptional places are worth a voyage of their own: a great silver lode, a rich silver vein, a silver seam, a mercury lode and a rich fishery.
[/list]

The Old World remains unchanged.

[h2]▶ How to play[/h2]
This download contains a complete, ready-to-play world. Subscribe, enable this map in your playset and start a new 1337 campaign. You do not need to run or enable the RNW generator to play it.

Use one RNW world at a time. Restart EU5 when switching maps, and keep this world mod for its saves.

Generator compatibility: EU5 1.4.*. New patches in this branch are usually compatible without waiting for a generator update; latest fully verified: 1.4.7. This ready-made map was generated with RNW 1.2.0 on EU5 1.4.7, so continue its campaigns on that exact game version. Across the Pillars is optional.

